      "message": "fix(3d): enable 3D Finish verify gate and fix exposed gouges\n\nRemove ungenerated pocket op R1 and tool EM-0600-4FL from the\nshared_face_bodies_finish fixture so verify runs across all six Z-bands\nof sample_ap214.step. Add explicit asserts that gate.skipped and\ngate.not_judged are absent, zero gouges occur, gate.ok is true, and\nS1 records its true shank_hit finding on 118 mm stock.\n\nFix three 3D finishing bugs exposed by active verify coverage:\n- Sample shallow-edge ellipse chords using exact cos_min^3 curvature\n  (MAX_CHORD = 0.006 mm) and exact theta = 0 slice crossings in scan.rs.\n- Trim 3-axis ring and steep-shallow runs against overhead canopies and\n  tight wall V-notches in rings_overhang.rs while keeping 5-axis swarf\n  under-equator rings untrimmed.\n- Cap raster_pass_spaced eps_chord at 0.005 mm (half DEV_TOL) so off-center\n  convex ridge chords stay within simulation tolerance.\n\nRecord the design choices in docs/decisions/1840-finish-verify-gate.md.\n\nChangelog: Fix 3D Finish shallow-edge, overhang-trim, and convex-chord gouges and run verify across all sample Z-bands\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #1840",
